               <p xml:id="idm133">Henrik Rung (1807-1871) was a Danish composer, conductor and singing teacher. He was a member of The Royal Danish Orchestra and later also singing master at the Royal Theatre. During a visit to Italy in 1837, he became very interested in Renaissance music, which in 1851 inspired him to found Cæciliaforeningens Madrigalkor, Denmark's most important mixed choir in the second part of the 19th century. In the 1890s Hartmann wrote several works for this ensemble, when Henrik Rung's son, Frederik Rung, had taken over as conductor of his father's choir.</p>
            </history>
